<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12307" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dāmon</span></b> , ōnis,
			m.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δάμων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Pythagorean, celebrated on account of the
				friendship between him and Phintias</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Off.
				3, 10, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 4,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An Athenian musician, teacher of Socrates</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Epam.
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A goat-herd</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 3,
				17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 1</span></i> sq.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
